config DEV_USB
    bool "USB developer access"
    default y if BOARD_UNAWATCH && !BOARD_UNAWATCH_LAB && (!RELEASE || BOARD_UNAWATCH_TETHER_SLOT)
    depends on BOARD_UNAWATCH
    select USB_DEVICE
    select USB_CDC_ACM
    select KERNEL_SYS_WORKQ
    help
      Two serial ports on the USB-C connector, behind the "USB developer"
      toggle of Settings > System > Debugging (off by default): the
      console, with the logs and the shell, and the tether protocol of
      tools/una/tether, which tether.py speaks to the stub too. Whoever
      plugs a cable in while it is on can read and write memory: see the
      decision log (docs/boards/unawatch/decisions). The USB is powered
      up only while the toggle is on and, unless DEV_USB_FOLLOW_VBUS is
      off, the watch is plugged in.

if DEV_USB

config DEV_USB_FORCE
    bool "Always on"
    default y if BOARD_UNAWATCH_TETHER_SLOT
    help
      The developer access stays on whatever the toggle says, plugged in
      or not. For images linked for the tether stub's slot, flashed and
      started through the stub, which grants the same access: the host
      that flashed one keeps its console and its tether port across
      settings that would turn them off.

config DEV_USB_FOLLOW_VBUS
    bool "Only while plugged in"
    default y
    depends on !DEV_USB_FORCE
    help
      Power the USB up only while the charger sees an input, as the
      PMIC reports it, and down at the unplug: the PHY and the 16 MHz
      crystal draw nothing on battery.

config DEV_USB_TETHER
    bool "Tether protocol"
    default y
    depends on SOC_STM32U5
    help
      The tether stub's protocol (tools/una/tether/stub/proto.c, built
      from there) on the second port: info, memory reads and writes,
      fill and CRC, I2C and GPIO, with the stub's refusals, notes, and
      reset and power-off. Calls of code and flashing are left to the
      stub: tether.py goes through a reset to it to flash.

config DEV_USB_THREAD_PRIO
    int "Tether thread priority"
    default 2
    depends on DEV_USB_TETHER

module = DEV_USB
module-str = USB developer access
source "subsys/logging/Kconfig.template.log_level"

endif # DEV_USB
